Z||000001||kslish||05-26-2001||04:07 AM||||That V6 engine is basically the Northstar/Aurora V8 engine with 2 cylinders lopped off, so the conversion would probably be pretty much like a Northstar conversion.  The reason the swap hasn't been done (as far as I know) is probably because if you're going to go through all that trouble, why not just go with a Northstar?  Although if you get the engine cheap enough, it may be worth it...but that engine is probably too new for them to be plentiful at the bone yards yet.<P>Ken S.<BR>'87GT and '86SC<BR> <A HREF="http://www.westpennfiero.org" TARGET=_blank>www.westpennfiero.org</A> <BR><p>[This message has been edited by kslish (edited 05-26-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Will||05-26-2001||05:51 PM||||If I were a betting man I might bet that the electronics are not significantly more complicated than what's associated with a 3800 swap.<P>But I'm not a betting man.||||reg||1
